import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="sempods concepts — a common interface for linked knowledge"
  description="Explore graph retrieval, authorization, identity, MCP and HTTP CRUD: the concepts that let different clients work with data in a pod."
  schemaType="TechArticle"
>
  <p class="eyebrow">concepts</p>
  <h1>Find knowledge. Follow links. Respect permissions.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A pod gives apps and agents a common way to use linked data. These concepts
    explain what they can do with it, and where the pod draws the boundary.
  </p>
  <div class="concept-list">
    <article>
      <h2><a href="/concepts/graph-retrieval">Graph retrieval</a></h2>
      <p>Find a useful starting point, follow resource links and build the graph your task needs.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2><a href="/concepts/context-permissions">Context permissions</a></h2>
      <p>The current contract's authorization boundary: one resource can have public and private depth.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2><a href="/concepts/federated-grants">Identity and grants</a></h2>
      <p>Recognize who is acting and what they may do, without making each app the account system.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2><a href="/concepts/mcp-over-pods">MCP over pods</a></h2>
      <p>Give agents a tool interface to independent data spaces, with each pod's authorization intact.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2><a href="/concepts/linked-data-crud">Linked Data CRUD</a></h2>
      <p>Read and write HTTP-addressed resources through an interface you can inspect.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p>
    These pages explain the ideas. The <a href="https://spec.sempods.org">development specification</a>{' '}defines the contract; the Kotlin release guides describe one implementation.
    Proposed changes are marked separately.
  </p>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href="/concepts/graph-retrieval">Start with retrieval</a>{' '}
    <a href="/start">Try a pod</a>
  </p>
</Base>
